Role/Tools.pm:602-609 / Chat.pm _gather_tools: tools with the same name from two MCP servers are both pushed into @all_tools (the map keeps the last server), so the request carries two identical function names (Anthropic/Gemini reject duplicates; advisor for OpenAI). Repro: two fake servers both offering "search" -> wire tools "search(a),search(b)".

Role/Tools.pm:652-653 (Chat.pm:382,463 same): a call to a name no server has (a hallucinated tool, or a malformed call where extract_tool_call returns undef -> "Tool '' not found" plus uninitialized warnings) dies after earlier calls of the same batch already executed; their results are lost and the model never learns the name is wrong. Repro: tool_calls [echo, web_search] -> echo runs, then die "Tool 'web_search' not found on any MCP server".

Fix: croak (or dedupe with a carp) at gather time on a duplicate name; answer an unknown/undef name with an is_error ToolResult ("unknown tool X") and continue the loop, matching the call_tool error path at l.655-661.
